    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34483" root="فلح" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَلَحَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَلَحٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>A</i> [<i>field,</i> or <i>land, such
as is termed</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرَاح</span>, (AHn, L, K,) <i>furrowed,</i> or
<i>ploughed, for cultivation:</i> its pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَلَحَات</span>, occurs
in a verse of Hassán, as some relate it; but

as others relate it, it is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَلَجَات</span>, with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ج</span>.
(AHn, L.)

